# macOS / Python noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# runtime outputs (key savestates are force-added)
traces/
# ASSET POLICY (maintainer ruling, 2026-08-04):
#   * SCREENSHOTS / game imagery -> NEVER tracked (see the image block below).
#   * SAVESTATES (.mss) -> KEPT, force-added, deliberately. They do embed WRAM
#     and VRAM, so strictly they carry game data — but they are not directly
#     accessible copyrighted content the way a picture is (inert without an
#     emulator and a matching ROM), and 152 files call loadSavestate: the demos
#     and several regression tests load them by name, so dropping them would
#     break the suites for a fresh clone. Judged a fair trade.
#   * If imagery ever HAS to be kept, the plan is two repos — a clean public one
#     and a private one holding savestates and other assets.

# local toolchain drops (never tracked; see HANDOFF §2 / docs)
tools/Mesen.app/
tools/mesen.zip
tools/Mesen.app.zip
tools/*.cpp
tools/Dispel/
tools/Flips/
vendor/
mockups/

# ROMs — copyrighted, never track, under ANY name or extension
roms/
*.sfc
*.smc
*.fig

# SCREENSHOTS AND ANY OTHER GAME IMAGERY — copyrighted, never track (2026-08-04).
# Emulator screenshots are game art just as much as a ROM is. They are evidence
# for a session, not repo content: probes write them under traces/ and they stay
# local. `git add -f` is NOT the escape hatch — nine had been force-added past
# the traces/ rule and were pushed before this. Precedent: mockups/ was purged
# from history in 2026-07-24 for exactly this reason.
# A genuinely ORIGINAL diagram (ours, no game art) may be force-added deliberately.
# Verified when this rule landed: all 107 .png opens in tools/ are "wb" — the
# toolchain WRITES screenshots and never reads one, so nothing in the harness
# depends on them being tracked.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp

# GAME AUDIO — same category as the imagery above. Decoded voice/sfx samples and
# ARAM dumps are game data; they are session evidence, sent to the maintainer for
# listening tests and kept local. Never tracked.
*.wav
*.brr
*.spc
*aram*.bin

# build/ holds only patch files: ignore everything, allow-list .bps/.ips back in
build/*
!build/*.bps
!build/*.ips

# archives (distribution zips are generated; force-add deliberately if ever needed)
*.zip
